  "number": 384,
  "title": "Shuffle an Array",
  "spec": "leetcode",
  "statement": "Write a class `Solution` around an integer array `nums` whose values are all different:\n\n- `Solution(nums)` stores the array.\n- `shuffle()` returns the values of `nums` in a random order, where each of the `n!` possible orders has the same chance of being returned.\n- `reset()` returns the array in the exact order the constructor received it.\n\nUse `Math.random()` for randomness; it is seeded here, so every run is repeatable. Because answers are random, the judge accepts any valid order, and on cases with many calls it also checks that the orders are spread evenly over the positions (a fixed or lopsided shuffle fails).",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= nums.length <= 50",
    "-10^6 <= nums[i] <= 10^6",
    "All values in nums are distinct.",
    "At most 10^4 calls in total are made to reset and shuffle."
